    {
      "id": "stock_radiant",
      "name": "Stock CoD Radiant",
      "source": "docs/research/07_editor_feel_reference.md section 4 (Hotkeys), column 'Stock default (binary)'; section 5a for Undo/Redo. An editor command is mapped only where the doc names the same action (e.g. HideUnSelected -> HideUnselected, MakeDetail -> BrushMakeDetail, SelectConnectedEntities -> SelectConnected, RotateZ -> RotateZ). The doc's '~' is written as '`' (the same grave key as the default). Not mapped, so they keep the IW8 default: patch row/column keys (the doc names them Plus/Subtract, numpad keys), SaveAs, PickMaterial, MakeNonColliding (its Ctrl+Shift+Minus is taken by a default), and every command with no stock row.",
